            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked whether, at the time SORNA was passed, almost all States had some kind of registration act."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0273efe9385e019c653995a0116a2becbb2f0aee709aa8102f038ec12f1e1607",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0273efe9385e-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked whether after SORNA some States would have less extensive coverage than others."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0273efe9385e019c653995a0116a2becbb2f0aee709aa8102f038ec12f1e1607",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0273efe9385e-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer also asked about the purpose of SORNA, noting a House report that the statute aims to help locate 100,000 missing people."
